      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-18",
        "notes": "Read Example, F1–F4, Verification 1.1–4.1 and all four direct suppliers after the level-4 limit review. Depth cap 1 and m=1 of p=2 satisfy the repaired algorithm domain. The four size-2 ordered bootstrap draws give pure count probabilities 1/4 each and mixed count probability 1/2. Pure samples return the corresponding label; mixed samples split at 1/2, and the independent uniform root feature routes (1/4,1/4) to labels 0 and 1 respectively. Thus the class-1 probability is 1/2 and the point-mass test margin is zero. Odd IID forest sizes have a symmetric binomial vote count with no tie, giving expected conditional error 1/2. If those bounded errors converged a.s. to zero, DCT on the randomization probability space would force their means to zero, a contradiction. This excludes a.s. convergence to zero and makes no stronger claim about existence of other limits. Both TikZ trees have the correct coordinate labels, left/right split convention and leaf labels (feature 1: 0,1; feature 2: 1,0); the rigorous count proof is independent of the diagrams. Breiman Theorem 1.2 p. 7 and Appendix I pp. 29–30 were read: they supply vote-frequency context and cannot remove this zero-margin caveat. No defect or AC use."
      }
