        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-18",
        "notes": "Read Example, F1–F5, Verification 1.1–3.1 and all five direct suppliers after the level-4 bound review. The prescribed two-stump law is a randomized-tree law, not a claim that arbitrary bagging data yield these weights. With test masses 3/4,1/4 and independent stump masses 3/4,1/4, the margins are 1/2,-1/2 and strength/error are both 1/4. Raw-margin means are +/-1/2, each second moment 1 and variance 3/4, hence d^2=3/4>0. Independent pair masses 9/16,1/16,6/16 multiply covariances 3/4,3/4,-3/4 to give 3/16; rho=1/4 and bound=15/4. The bound may exceed 1 without being false; the displayed error is 1/4. All finite spaces are measurable, s>0 and d>0 meet the bound's hypotheses, and there are two classes and no zero margin. Breiman Definitions 2.1–2.2 and Theorem 2.3, printed pp. 8–9, supply the contextual conventions, independently proved in the local supplier. No defect, diagram or AC use; only the algorithm's unchanged unit-vote convention is consumed."
